    "gold_justification": "Double-blind RCT with n>3500 and 3-year follow-up. Authors explicitly call the effect\n'modest', acknowledge demographic limitations, and call for more diverse studies.\nThe reporting matches the evidence strength — no overclaim.\n",
    "gold_alternative_reading": "The effect size is very small (0.2-word difference from placebo). One could argue this\napproaches 'clinically negligible' territory, but the authors frame it honestly. An\noverclaim reading would require the authors to inflate the finding, which they do not.\n",
    "gold_case_type": "clear",
    "curator_notes": "Tests whether agents can distinguish a modest-but-honest finding from overclaim.\nThe trap is small effect size — agents may overflag. Both sprints show stable\ncorrect classification, with occasional FP on 'overclaim' keyword mentions.\n"
